Subject: [PATCH] ap: expose WDS encryption setup to deferred authorization

The deferred WDS setup in sta_info.c calls hostapd_set_wds_encryption,
but ieee802_11.c still defines it as static. Shared-library linking accepts
the resulting unresolved external reference, which fails at runtime when
the deferred WDS setup succeeds. Export the existing implementation and
declare it in the header already included by both callers. Preserve the
real encryption behavior and the post-authorization ordering.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [companion to local deferred WDS setup]

--- a/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -6466,3 +6466,3 @@
-static void hostapd_set_wds_encryption(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
-				       struct sta_info *sta,
-				       char *ifname_wds)
+void hostapd_set_wds_encryption(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
+			      struct sta_info *sta,
+			      char *ifname_wds)
--- a/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.h
+++ b/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.h
@@ -27,3 +27,5 @@
 
+void hostapd_set_wds_encryption(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
+			      struct sta_info *sta, char *ifname_wds);
 int ieee802_11_mgmt(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *buf, size_t len,
 		    struct hostapd_frame_info *fi);
